  "divergences": {
    "_divergences_are": "Where OUR engine deliberately differs from the reference. A divergence declares the RULE of the difference, not the expected output: `strip` is a regex that removes exactly what we add, and the suite requires the remainder to equal the reference BYTE FOR BYTE. Nothing here stores a rendered blob, so there is nothing to re-record and no place to hide an unrelated regression — any other drift breaks the equality. An entry that strips nothing in any of its cases fails as stale.",
    "unknown-type-placeholder": {
      "task": "SDL-608",
      "reason": "A node whose type is not in the registry draws a placeholder instead of returning null. The reference loses the node and its whole subtree silently, which is how a published page goes blank when an export is renamed away.",
      "strip": "<div class=\"ss-unknown-type-placeholder\"[^>]*>[^<]*</div>",
